-- Q1764: Review and Compilation [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Issue a compilation report with the omission clearly indicated in the report","Decline to issue a compilation report under any circumstances","Issue a standard compilation report without any modifications","Convert the engagement to a review engagement instead"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AR-C 80, the accountant may compile financial statements that omit substantially all disclosures provided the omission is clearly indicated in the report and is not intended to mislead users. This is common for internal-use statements.
Wrong (B): AR-C 80 does not prohibit compilation when disclosures are omitted. The standard specifically permits it with proper disclosure of the omission.
Wrong (C): A standard report without modification would fail to alert users that substantially all disclosures have been omitted.
Wrong (D): The accountant is not required to change the engagement level; compilation with noted omissions is acceptable under AR-C 80.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1764;

-- Q1769: Review and Compilation [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
