  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AR-C 80.20, a compilation report is typically addressed to management, the board of directors, or those charged with governance of the entity, unless the engagement terms specify otherwise.
Wrong (B): The SEC is a regulatory body. Compilation reports for nonissuers are not filed with or addressed to the SEC.
Wrong (C): While creditors may receive copies, the report is addressed to the entity''s management or governance, not to external parties like lenders.
Wrong (D): The AICPA is a professional organization that sets standards but is not the intended recipient of compilation reports.$EXPL$
