-- Q1771: Review and Compilation [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Perform additional procedures including further inquiries to resolve the matter","Immediately withdraw from the engagement without further action","Issue a qualified review report without performing further procedures","Convert the engagement to a compilation to reduce scope"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AR-C 90.36-.37, when the accountant believes the financial statements may be materially misstated, the accountant must perform additional procedures sufficient to obtain limited assurance. These include additional inquiries and possibly other procedures to resolve the matter.
Wrong (B): Immediate withdrawal is not the first step. The accountant should attempt to resolve the matter through additional procedures before considering withdrawal.
Wrong (C): Issuing a qualified report without performing further procedures would not satisfy the accountant''s responsibility to obtain limited assurance under AR-C 90.
Wrong (D): Converting to a compilation is not appropriate simply because a potential misstatement is identified; the accountant should first attempt resolution.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1771;

-- Q1772: Review and Compilation [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["A separate accountant''s report attached to the statements","A legend stating no assurance is provided on the statements","The CPA firm''s official letterhead on each page","A statement certifying the statements comply with GAAP"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under AR-C 70.07, when no report is issued for a preparation engagement, each page of the financial statements must include a legend such as "no assurance is provided on these financial statements." This alerts users that no audit, review, or compilation procedures were performed.
Wrong (A): A preparation engagement is distinguished from a compilation precisely because no separate report is issued. The legend replaces the report.
Wrong (C): Including the CPA firm''s letterhead is not a requirement under AR-C 70 and does not communicate the level of service provided.
Wrong (D): The legend does not certify GAAP compliance. It communicates the absence of assurance, not the framework used.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1772;

-- Q1777: Review and Compilation [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Proceed with the limited review and modify the report accordingly","Evaluate whether the limitation prevents a complete review and withdraw if so","Downgrade the engagement to a compilation engagement automatically","Issue a standard review report and document the limitation internally"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under AR-C 90.44-.45, if management imposes a limitation that prevents the accountant from performing procedures considered necessary, the accountant must consider whether this results in an incomplete review. If the review cannot be completed, withdrawal is appropriate.
Wrong (A): The accountant cannot simply proceed with a limited review and modify the report. A scope limitation in a review may make the engagement incomplete, not merely modified.
Wrong (C): Automatic downgrade to a compilation is not permitted. Any change in engagement level must follow the requirements of AR-C 90.46 regarding reasonable justification.
Wrong (D): Issuing a standard report while merely documenting the limitation internally would misrepresent the scope of work performed.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1777;

-- Q1781: Review and Compilation [hard/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The prior-year compiled statements must be re-compiled under the review standards","The prior-year compiled statements may accompany the reviewed statements with proper reference","The prior-year statements must be audited before comparative presentation","The prior-year statements cannot be presented alongside reviewed statements"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under AR-C 90.56, when comparative financial statements are presented with different levels of service, the prior-year compiled statements may be presented alongside the current-year reviewed statements. The compilation report should be reissued or referenced in the current-year report.
Wrong (A): The prior-year statements do not need to be re-compiled. They may be presented at their original service level with appropriate reference to the compilation.
Wrong (C): AR-C does not require the prior-year statements to be audited for comparative presentation. Different service levels may coexist in comparative statements.
Wrong (D): There is no prohibition on presenting compiled and reviewed statements together. AR-C specifically contemplates this scenario.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1781;

-- Q1794: Review/Compilation Engagements [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Only if all required disclosures are eventually included in full","If the selected disclosures are not misleading and the omission is disclosed","Only if the entity qualifies as a nonprofit organization","It is never acceptable to include selected disclosures with omissions"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under AR-C 80.22, selected disclosures may be included in compiled financial statements that omit substantially all disclosures, provided they are not misleading and the report clearly states the omission. Including selected notes does not imply completeness.
Wrong (A): AR-C 80 does not require that all disclosures eventually be included. The standard permits selective inclusion alongside the omission disclosure.
Wrong (C): The entity type is irrelevant. AR-C 80.22 applies to all entities, not just nonprofits.
Wrong (D): AR-C 80 expressly permits selected disclosures in statements omitting substantially all disclosures, provided they are not misleading.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1794;

-- Q1796: Review/Compilation Engagements [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Discuss the matter with management and consider the effect on the issued report","Take no action since the review report has already been issued","Issue an audit report on the revised financial statements instead","Notify the SEC directly about the discovered misstatement"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AR-C 90.A66, when the accountant becomes aware of subsequently discovered information indicating a material misstatement, the accountant should discuss the matter with management, request revision if appropriate, and consider whether users need to be informed about the impact on the review report.
Wrong (B): Ignoring material subsequently discovered information would violate the accountant''s professional obligations under AR-C 90.
Wrong (C): The accountant does not convert a review to an audit. The appropriate response is to address the misstatement within the existing review framework.
Wrong (D): Notifying the SEC is not the accountant''s obligation for nonissuer review engagements. The accountant works with management to correct the statements.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1796;

-- Q1797: Review/Compilation Engagements [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["When there is reasonable justification such as changed circumstances or requirements","Only if the accountant has not yet begun the review procedures","It is never acceptable to downgrade from a review to a compilation","Only if the client agrees to pay the full original review fee"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AR-C 90.46, a change from a review to a compilation may be acceptable when there is reasonable justification, such as changed circumstances, changed requirements, or a misunderstanding of the service originally requested. However, AR-C 90.47 states the accountant should not agree if the change appears intended to avoid disclosure.
Wrong (B): The timing of review procedures is not the determining factor. The key consideration is whether there is a reasonable justification for the change.
Wrong (C): AR-C 90.46 explicitly contemplates acceptable circumstances for changing from a review to a compilation engagement.
Wrong (D): Fee arrangements are not a criterion for evaluating whether a change in engagement level is appropriate.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1797;

-- Q1799: Review/Compilation Engagements [medium/L2]
